# DeutschChat — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values.
# `.env.local` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# The app compiles and runs without these set; anything that talks to Supabase
# shows a clear "not configured" state until they are filled in.

# --- Supabase (hosted project) --------------------------------------------
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API.
# On Vercel, the Supabase integration provisions these automatically — confirm
# the names in Vercel -> Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables. The app
# needs exactly these four; the browser bundle only ever gets the two
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ values (anon key + URL).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project-ref.supabase.co"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-anon-public-key"

# Project Settings -> API -> "service_role" secret.
# SERVER ONLY. Bypasses Row Level Security. Never expose to the client,
# never commit. Currently used only by scripts/admin helpers.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="your-service-role-secret"

# --- App -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Public base URL. Used for auth email redirect links (/auth/callback).
# Locally: http://localhost:3000. On Vercel: your production origin.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# --- Supabase CLI (shell env, NOT loaded by Next) -----------------------
# Needed to run `npm run db:*` against the hosted project:
#   export SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=...      # https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens
#   npx supabase link --project-ref your-project-ref
#   npx supabase db push --include-seed   # apply migrations + curriculum seed
#   npm run db:types                      # regenerate types/database.ts
#
# `npm run db:check` verifies a live connection using the NEXT_PUBLIC_* +
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY values above.
